Fix par task test race condition\\n\\nIn TestTasks we have test to ensure that tasks composed with `par` are\\nrun in parallel. The test makes the assumption that setting a value for\\nthe promise returned from a task will immediately set the value for the\\ntask itself. However, there is a gap between returning a promise and\\nhooking up the promise listener which allows for a race.\\n\\nThis change eliminates the race by waiting for the par task to complete.\\nAlternatively, we could have waited for task 2 to complete, but this\\napproach is more general and less sensitive to changes.
